 "_about": "The map surfaces as 0.69d has them (the owner, 2026-11-16: \"let's not change things unless 0.69 does so\"; docs/notes/sound-gaps.md 1.8 and 2). A triangle's material is its face name's game_material_settings/<name>/game_material_id in its model's settings, read when the collision is cooked (collision_shape_cook 0x82590); the material is the step's and the bullet's (its armor, ricochet, pierce), so this changes what a match computes (simulation_changes.tsv). The Chemical Plant's tracks: 0.69d has no props/railroad/railroad.model, a second mesh of the whole track bed (cgroup 10, cmask 20h, every face metall_tank) over railroad_01..03, which cover the same bed; its collision object goes from the 15 level_04 projects (the drawn model stays), and railroad_01..03's rails (coll_metal_thick_s) are metall_tank (55) as 0.69d's settings have them (0.26g: metall_thick_walkable 71). Faces with no material that 0.69d's settings name: Radar's garage_inside (metall_thick, concrete, gravel, metall_thin, wood_silent) and the Fort's center_part_01_floor (gravel, ground; its walker face ground). The names stay as they are (\"not assigned or deleted\", \"metall_thick_walkable\"): the cook reads the id. Mamayev's monument and statue_ground, the Fort's out_wall_base_a_2, London's building_07_3 and building_06_1_indoor_01's stucco have no material in 0.69d either and stay as they are. Vector's centre_lab_dome (its one face name, 'default', has no entry in 0.26g's settings: 3FFFh) gets 0.69d's entry, the material default (11).",
